<title>HONG KONG: HK Observatory reports quake north of Japan.</title>
<headline>HK Observatory reports quake north of Japan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>An intense earthquake was recorded off northern Japan about 200 km west of Sapporo, the Royal Hong Kong Observatory said.</p>
<p>The quake, estimated to be 6.0 on the Richter scale, was recorded at 10.59 p.m. on Sunday (1459 GMT).</p>
<p>The epicentre was initially determined to be off the western coast of northern Japan west of Sapporo, Hokkaido, at 43.2 N 138.9 E, the observatory said.</p>
